WEBVTT

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.130
That thief ran in the opposite direction!

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:43.240
He’s wounded!

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:44.400
Don’t let him get away!

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:57.350
Come in.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:05.620
Is it okay to help a thief, Ichi-san?

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:09.410
The thief disappeared around here.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:10.750
We’ll conduct a search.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.030
Hide.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:17.490
Ichi-san!

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.950
There’s blood on the window.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:22.910
Stab me with your hairpin.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.400
Do it.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.880
We want to search your room.

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:30.340
He’s bleeding!

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:34.090
The police are called in for lovers’ quarrels now?

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:40.230
He promised to buy my freedom,

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:42.900
yet he was seeing other women as well!

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:47.340
He trampled on my feelings!

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:52.800
I’m sorry. I won’t do it again.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.650
You’re the only one for me.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:55.980
Come here.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:02.660
It’s not a big enough deal to involve the police.

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:06.120
That’s downright idiotic.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.120
Let’s check the next room.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:12.640
Ichi-san, are you all right?

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:14.690
I stabbed you a bit too deeply.

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:17.700
We will treat him first.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:18.650
Get the medicines.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.260
She stabbed my stomach.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:34.060
She got too carried away.

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:41.090
What’s your name?

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.150
Yaichi.

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:44.490
If there’s anything I...

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.540
No need.

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:51.120
Why the long face?

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:55.510
Is there a particular reason why you need money?

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:06.360
After handing over the money, you received a letter from the Five Leaves

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:10.450
that said they’d return Yuutarou in a few days?

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.990
This is for your services through today.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:19.130
Work is work.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:23.170
I won’t be stingy about paying you.

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:26.800
However, this also means that your work here is finished.

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:32.970
Masa.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:42.480
Oomiya is involved with the rising prices of rice by cornering the market.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:43.910
They paid for your services?

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:52.560
You’re going to send that, along with your share from this job, to your family, right?

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:00.120
Go home and take a break.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.160
Welcome, Masa-san.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.240
Ume-dono.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:21.060
When are you going to visit the old man?

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:22.210
Tomorrow.

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:24.820
Would you mind if I go with you?

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:37.500
Where’s Yuutarou-dono?

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:40.900
He’s in a trunk in the closet.

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:49.870
Actually, Ichi told me not to bring you here.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:53.100
Did you get attached to him or something?

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:57.390
Don’t worry. I’ll return him safely later.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:59.160
Go and cut the leeks now.

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:03.550
How many jobs have you done now?

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:05.580
Less than ten.

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:11.110
I’ve been wanting to get out of this business, but this is where I grew up.

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:12.090
I have no other choice.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:15.810
You don’t think of the Five Leaves as chivalrous bandits?

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:18.870
That’s what I say when Okinu is around.

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:22.520
At first, we began to fight against wrongdoers,

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:26.070
but now, we are nothing more than bandits.

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:27.720
We do this for the money.

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:31.560
I know nothing about your circumstances.

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:34.780
You didn’t hear anything from Yaichi-dono?

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:36.240
No.

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:40.770
Did he tell you about himself after hearing your story?

00:06:41.090 --> 00:06:41.960
No.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:44.240
Of course not.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:47.070
He never talks about himself.

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:55.050
Yaichi-dono is enigmatic in many ways.

00:06:56.290 --> 00:07:00.310
He likes mind games.

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:03.070
You can’t tell what’s on his mind.

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:08.790
That ronin has secluded himself in his home again.

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:10.200
Seems like he’s working from home.

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:17.480
I have to send the money back home as soon as possible, but...

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:19.790
Hey there.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.980
Are you going to sell paper lanterns?

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:27.910
Here’s your share from the last job.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:36.810
I’m not sure if it’s okay to accept this money and send it to my family.

00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:42.070
Besides, I didn’t work as a member.

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:44.860
I can’t accept this as a reward.

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:48.400
You’re depending on it, aren’t you?

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:52.240
We won’t have another job for a while.

00:07:52.970 --> 00:07:55.090
Will you make paper lanterns until then?

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:01.380
Follow me.

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:11.720
Are you the highly skilled bodyguard Ichi was talking about?

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:15.660
We’ll clean up the storage room, so you can sleep there.

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:19.740
I’ll see, with my own eyes, whether or not you are useful.

00:08:20.510 --> 00:08:22.690
Um, excuse me.

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:27.020
And I’ll let Ichi tell you how to handle the girls.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:33.160
Yaichi-dono, when did you start living here?

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:35.360
It’s been so long...

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.090
I forgot already.

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:38.660
But...

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:42.830
You have a personality that’s easily tricked by women.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:44.660
You’re naive and don’t doubt people.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:49.390
Watch out for the girls here.

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:53.120
Also, Matsu comes here from time to time.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.140
How’s the situation at Oomiya?

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:00.760
Nothing special.

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:04.060
The kid didn’t seem to grasp what happened.

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:07.950
His mother told him about the kidnapping.

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:13.190
She said the bodyguard was too useless to even babysit.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:16.580
I’ll be going.

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:17.120
Okay.

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:24.570
Are you worried about that kid?

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:29.050
I was completely unaware that he was adopted.

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:31.480
I just started working there recently,

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:36.510
and he seemed to feel lonely because of his strict mother.

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:40.850
I feel bad about kidnapping him after he’s gone through so much.

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:41.520
Masa.

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:45.440
That’s boring.

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:53.950
You’re nice.

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:57.770
Anyway, you better get used to this soon.

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:08.630
I’ve been pondering this for a few days now.

00:10:08.870 --> 00:10:12.100
You’re someone who doesn’t show his feelings.

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:17.720
Yet, when I asked about your objectives, you answered without hesitation.

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:23.060
You don’t care about the money, right?

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:29.070
Sensei.

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:32.950
Your room is ready.

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:34.980
Thank you.

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:50.700
If I stay here, I might learn something new about Yaichi-dono.

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:05.290
I’m so tired. My legs feel heavy.

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:12.590
I never imagined that I’d be living in a brothel.

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:24.090
The toilet must have been cold, no?

00:11:33.030 --> 00:11:35.490
Don’t cause a fuss here.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:39.150
I just got into his bed.

00:11:39.150 --> 00:11:42.530
Didn’t I tell you not to get involved with him?

00:11:42.530 --> 00:11:46.040
We can’t possibly leave a young man like him alone, can we?

00:11:46.630 --> 00:11:49.040
And you should get a hold of yourself.

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:52.050
You’ll trouble me if you cause a fuss over such trivial things.

00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:53.260
Ichi!

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:55.150
Ichi!

00:11:56.970 --> 00:12:00.420
Sheesh, what kind of guy did you bring here?

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:04.100
You said you would see how he does for a while, didn’t you?

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:07.610
What are you doing in his room?

00:12:07.610 --> 00:12:10.420
I couldn’t find a customer who’d sleep over here.

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:14.530
Haven’t I always told you not to go to this room?

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:19.500
Oh, come on. He’s paying me.

00:12:19.770 --> 00:12:22.230
Go back to your room now.

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:23.140
You, too.

00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:24.910
Okay, ma’am.

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:32.970
Get your act together.

00:12:32.970 --> 00:12:34.650
Y-Yes.

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:54.690
You don’t care about the money, right?

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:03.930
This is boring. I like him better when he’s dumb.

00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:12.950
Have you gotten used to this place yet, Sensei?

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:14.980
How could he in just three days?

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:17.970
Sensei, do you have someone?

00:13:17.970 --> 00:13:19.090
No.

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:20.800
How about some sweets?

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:22.260
No, thanks.

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:24.940
Oh, don’t play polite with us.

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:26.940
No, really. I’m not hungry.

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:28.940
Hey, give me one.

00:13:32.070 --> 00:13:36.340
Ichi-san buys us all kinds of things.

00:13:36.340 --> 00:13:38.580
Just recently, he bought us sugar candy.

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:41.650
He’s quite generous.

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:47.050
The taboo question is: “Where does he get the money?”

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:50.590
Looks like you know more about him.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:52.290
Like his background and such.

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:55.200
We don’t need to know it.

00:13:55.820 --> 00:14:00.360
We all have our own circumstances.

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:04.390
It’s not nice to be nosy.

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:10.960
“Have you gotten used to this place yet, Sensei?”

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:12.580
“How could he in just three days?”

00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:16.240
Their voices can be heard clearly.

00:14:16.700 --> 00:14:18.620
Isn’t this place nice and lively?

00:14:20.190 --> 00:14:22.080
You don’t look well.

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:24.290
I feel like I have a cold.

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:26.410
I think I’m just tired.

00:14:27.750 --> 00:14:32.070
Otake is paying your rent in Nagaya. Rest assured.

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:36.730
Even if you got fired from here, you’d still have a home.

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:38.180
I see.

00:14:38.180 --> 00:14:39.430
But...

00:14:40.010 --> 00:14:43.910
She might move in there.

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:53.690
I thought I’d move in.

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:57.060
Let me stay here until I find another place.

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:01.460
I’ve been meaning to ask you...

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:05.160
Where did the name “Five Leaves” come from?

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:08.340
I decided on the name,

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:10.680
but you better ask Ichi-san about the reason.

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:14.160
Are you two old friends?

00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:18.490
Of the Five Leaves, I think I’ve known him the longest.

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:23.640
Ichi-san helped me in the past.

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:28.240
I’m hungry. Shall we go out and eat?

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:30.440
I must go back.

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:32.650
Then, I’ll accompany you.

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:41.770
Oh, my.

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:47.080
You don’t have much energy, do you?

00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:50.680
You should have lunch before going back to work.

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:51.860
Right...

00:15:53.950 --> 00:15:57.420
I talked with Masa about the rent earlier.

00:15:57.420 --> 00:15:59.590
So, I thought I’d pay my rent as well.

00:16:01.660 --> 00:16:03.080
This is for the next six months.

00:16:03.890 --> 00:16:06.340
That’s more than enough for six months.

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:12.780
I’ve still got some of the last “rent” you paid me.

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:20.000
Make hairpins for the girls or something.

00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:27.060
Why “Five Leaves”?

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:30.140
Otake came up with it.

00:16:30.140 --> 00:16:31.160
The reason?

00:16:31.780 --> 00:16:33.790
She said it was because she likes maple leaves.

00:16:35.740 --> 00:16:36.600
Matsu.

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:38.440
About Oomiya...

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:42.180
If there’s no change, you can stop watching them.

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:44.650
Come in.

00:16:46.450 --> 00:16:48.250
I’ll get you some tea.

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:50.330
No, I’ll be going now.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:52.880
Have something warm before you go.

00:17:00.610 --> 00:17:02.070
That’s unlike him.

00:17:04.970 --> 00:17:07.560
He usually doesn’t do anything without having a reason.

00:17:07.990 --> 00:17:13.570
He dislikes sentimentality, so he doesn’t butt into other people’s business either.

00:17:15.290 --> 00:17:17.530
He used to be like that.

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:19.150
Did he change?

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:25.530
Have you known him for a long time?

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:30.640
He did me a big favor in the past.

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:37.250
Matsukichi-dono left already.

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:03.280
That’s how he is.

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:13.980
You want to know more about me, right?

00:18:15.750 --> 00:18:18.690
Are you interested in my personality?

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:24.990
Or my background?

00:18:30.810 --> 00:18:33.020
Personality.

00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:37.580
I see.

00:18:37.580 --> 00:18:43.060
In that case, I hope we will have a long relationship.

00:18:52.660 --> 00:18:56.190
I’ll go patrol outside.

00:18:58.870 --> 00:19:00.040
Are your legs numb?

00:19:00.710 --> 00:19:03.980
No, they just feel really heavy below the knees.

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:08.180
It hurts when I try to move them.

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:10.160
Good night.

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:22.700
Sensei, watch where you’re going!

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:26.490
He fell without tripping.

00:19:26.490 --> 00:19:28.950
Didn’t he say that he wasn’t hungry as well?

00:19:31.050 --> 00:19:35.180
I’ve heard of a disease called “Edo Disease.”

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:48.730
You can’t just murder him, Dad!

00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:49.400
Let go of me!

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:50.820
Dad!

00:19:52.780 --> 00:19:55.410
Oh, my. Showing authority?

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:59.040
Okinu-chan. You’re back.

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:04.090
They dismissed you from the job for the shogun’s vassal?

00:20:04.090 --> 00:20:05.280
Why?

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:08.350
The second son was trying to make a pass at her.

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:09.240
Oh, my.

00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:12.800
He was about to make an advance, but I refused him.

00:20:13.420 --> 00:20:17.030
After that, I was harassed,

00:20:17.030 --> 00:20:19.920
and they made me quit.

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:24.590
He’s going to marry into another vassal’s family, anyway.

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:30.930
That’s really ugly. To think he was trying to mess around before that.

00:20:32.590 --> 00:20:35.330
I won’t forgive anyone who makes Okinu cry!

00:20:35.850 --> 00:20:38.370
She was the only one who got hurt.

00:20:38.370 --> 00:20:40.000
How do you expect me to stay calm?!

00:20:40.200 --> 00:20:44.960
He’s marrying into another family with a dowry, right?

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:47.920
Why don’t you take that money?

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:50.020
Rob him?

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:56.840
We’ll kidnap him.

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:16.090
I’ve got a feeling that something was hidden

00:21:16.090 --> 00:21:25.380
in the words you once told me. Those words cross my mind again and again.

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:33.800
Yet your voice always sounds the same as before.

00:21:33.800 --> 00:21:40.850
Every time I breathe, I wanna hold you in my arms

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:49.780
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:57.860
Every time I breathe, I just wanna hold you in my arms again

00:21:58.980 --> 00:22:06.680
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:22:07.340 --> 00:22:14.920
Every day I need you  All the time I'll be there for you

00:22:15.650 --> 00:22:24.030
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:22:30.160 --> 00:22:33.200
Next time on House of Five Leaves:

00:22:33.700 --> 00:22:34.820
Okinu here.

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:40.320
For some reason, everyone who comes to my dad’s place is kind of strange.

00:22:40.890 --> 00:22:43.200
Who among them intrigues me?

00:22:43.200 --> 00:22:46.170
Well, that’s a secret.

00:22:46.790 --> 00:22:48.010
Well then, the next episode’s title is:

00:22:48.010 --> 00:22:49.880
“It’ll Be Fine.”
